## Decisions

### Nothing recent broke this — Helios Admin's sign-in page has never had its logo. Shall I cut Admin's brand files from the designer's exports so the sign-in page, favicon and home-screen icon work?

**What's happening.** Every app's sign-in page is one template (`web/templates/login.html`) that shows `<img src="/brand/logo-lockup-light.png" alt="Helios Admin">`. An app's public files come from `web/public/<app>/` (served before sign-in). There is no `web/public/admin/` folder in git, and there never has been (`git log --all -- web/public/admin` is empty). So on admin.heliosian.com, `/brand/logo-lockup-light.png` falls through to the sign-in page itself:

```
$ curl -sI https://admin.heliosian.com/brand/logo-lockup-light.png
HTTP/2 200
content-type: text/html; charset=utf-8
content-length: 8770        <- the sign-in page, not a PNG
```

The same is true of Admin's `/brand/icon-192.png`, favicons, splash screens and `/manifest.webmanifest`. You're normally signed in to Admin, so you'd only see it when the session lapses. Today's merges (a1b3d07, e644de6, 134a42a, 417eba6) don't touch this.

**What exists.** The designer's Admin art is already in the repo: `asset-sources/admin/exports/` holds `app icon.png`, `favicon.png`, `horizontal - teal/white.png`, `vertical - teal/white.png` and `symbol_white.png` (added 2026-10-03, updated 2026-10-05). Only `web/public/common/brand/apps/admin.png`, the mark in the app switch, was ever cut from them.

- (*) Cut the full set
  Create `web/public/admin/brand/` with the same files and widths as `web/public/mcp/brand/` (`favicon-16/32.png`, `icon-192/512.png`, `apple-touch-icon.png`, `maskable-icon-192/512.png`, `logo-mark.png`, `logo-tile.png`, `logo-lockup.png`, `logo-lockup-light.png`, `logo-lockup-horizontal.png`, `symbol-white.png`, and `splash/` with every size the template lists), cut per `docs/brand.md` with ImageMagick (I'll `brew install imagemagick`), plus `web/public/admin/manifest.webmanifest` copied from MCP's with the name "Helios Admin". Add `admin` to the app list in `docs/brand.md`. On the sign-in page, the "?" box becomes the white Admin vertical lockup, like every other app's. Then it needs a deploy to show on production.
- ( ) Only the sign-in logo
  Cut just `web/public/admin/brand/logo-lockup-light.png`. The broken box goes away, but the favicon, home-screen icon, splash screens and manifest stay missing.

ian@fc.run chose: Cut the full set
